            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0764" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg630"/>

                <head>No. 455.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Pendleton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-06">April 6, 1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 303.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 585, of the 22d of
                    February last, reporting your action in declining to issue a passport to Mr.
                    Frank Kessel, upon the ground of a discrepancy between his certificate of
                    naturalization and his passport, was duly received.</p>
                <p>A copy of your dispatch was communicated to the probate judge of Montgomery
                    County, who has furnished a corrected certificate, with the statement that the
                    clerical error in the paper furnished to Mr. Kessel was caused by the accidental
                    use of a wrong form of certificate.</p>
                <p>Inclosing the amended certificate of naturalization for the files of your
                    legation,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
